---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Minted & Gone">
  <div class="shell guide-page about-page">
    <section class="field-hero simple-hero compact-hero about-hero">
      <div class="hero-botanical" aria-hidden="true">☘</div>
      <div class="hero-copy plate-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About this archive</p>
        <h1>About Minted &amp; Gone</h1>
        <p class="lede">A static field guide for NFT marketplace histories.</p>
        <p>Minted &amp; Gone keeps a careful record of marketplace status, evidence, and what remains when platforms fade, close, merge, or change identity.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="mock-note">The current implementation uses mock layout records only. Treat the archive as a design and validation prototype until records are sourced and reviewed.</p>

    <section class="about-section-grid">
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">01</span>
        <h2>What is Minted &amp; Gone?</h2>
        <p>Minted &amp; Gone is a field-guide archive for NFT marketplaces. It uses static pages and JSON records to describe marketplace identity, status, evidence, and historical context.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">02</span>
        <h2>Why NFT marketplaces need an archive</h2>
        <p>NFT marketplaces can disappear unevenly: websites go dark, contracts remain readable, assets move to other interfaces, and announcements scatter across the web. An archive helps keep those changes reviewable.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">03</span>
        <h2>What this project tracks</h2>
        <p>Records track marketplace names, aliases, status, category, chain scope, frontend and contract state, asset visibility, timeline events, evidence notes, confidence, and review status.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">04</span>
        <h2>What this project does not do</h2>
        <p>It does not provide price data, wallet connection, login, rankings, legal analysis, investment advice, or real-time uptime monitoring. The archive is historical and source-oriented.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">05</span>
        <h2>Community corrections</h2>
        <p>Corrections should include source URLs, archive URLs when available, and precise notes about dates, status, or what remains. The goal is to make uncertainty visible rather than hide it.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card">
        <span class="num">06</span>
        <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>Minted &amp; Gone is not investment advice, not legal advice, and not a guarantee that any marketplace, URL, contract, or asset remains available at runtime.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="framed-panel definition-card about-cta">
      <p class="eyebrow">Field-guide, not dashboard</p>
      <h2>Designed for reviewable history</h2>
      <p>The archive intentionally uses static pages, JSON records, and visible uncertainty. That makes it easier to review claims and harder to mistake mock records for live market signals.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/methodology/">Read methodology</a><a class="btn" href="/submit/">Submit/correct</a></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
